  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For all nonzero numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) such that \\(x=\\frac{1}{y},\\) \\[ \\left(x-\\frac1x\\right)\\left(y+\\frac1y\\right) \\] equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2x^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x^2+y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^2-y^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(y^2-x^2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1978-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x=\\frac{1}{y},\\) we also have \\(y=\\frac{1}{x}.\\) Thus the product is \\[ (x-y)(y+x)=x^2-y^2. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the reciprocal relation to replace \\(\\frac{1}{x}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{y}\\)",
        "The two factors become \\(x-y\\) and \\(x+y\\)"
      ],
